@delflein I can not reproduce this issue.
Your values in the config are too low to create meaningful steps.
Try 0.3 as a cost for example, which is in $ per 1M tokens.

@nstoeckigt respecting x-litellm-response-cost headers is a different feature request.

Hi there, maintainer of obsidian-mcp-server here — wanted to share a few findings that might help narrow this down.

**Schema dump.** Here's the actual `inputSchema` the server emits for `obsidian_patch_note` (descriptions and a couple of optional fields elided for brevity), in case it's useful for comparison against what opencode is validating against:

```json
{
  "$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#",
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "target": {
      "oneOf": [
        {"type": "object", "properties": {"type": {"type": "string", "const": "path"}, "path": {"type": "string", "minLength": 1}}, "required": ["type", "path"]},
        {"type": "object", "properties": {"type": {"type": "string", "const": "active"}}, "required": ["type"]},
        {"type": "object", "properties": {"type": {"type": "string", "const": "periodic"}, "period": {"type": "string", "enum": ["daily","weekly","monthly","quarterly","yearly"]}}, "required": ["type", "period"]}
      ]
    },
    "section": {"type": "object", "properties": {"type": {"type": "string", "enum": ["heading","block","frontmatter"]}, "target": {"type": "string", "minLength": 1}}, "required": ["type", "target"]},
    "operation": {"type": "string", "enum": ["append","prepend","replace"]},
    "content": {"type": "string"}
  },
  "required": ["target", "section", "operation", "content"]
}
```

It's standard JSON Schema — `oneOf` with a `const` discriminator and nested `properties`. Both shapes are core features in draft-07 and JSON Schema 2020-12 (the [MCP spec default](https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2025-11-25/basic#json-schema-usage) when no `$schema` is set).

**One detail that might point at the cause.** The reporter mentions a `required property 'sectionTargeted'` error for `obsidian_append_to_note`. That field only exists in the tool's `outputSchema`, not its input — so the validator may be reading from the wrong schema (or a merged one) for tools with multiple nested-object parameters. That lines up with @r007b34r's flattening hypothesis.

Happy to provide full schema dumps for any of the affected tools or help test a fix against the live server.
